# Next.js is pinned to 15.2.3, below the fix version for these three
# CVEs (all denial-of-service class, not RCE/data-exposure), because
# @cloudflare/next-on-pages@1.13.16 (the latest release, as of
# 2026-08-08) cannot build ANY newer 15.x release, including 15.5.2 —
# its own declared peer-dependency ceiling. Verified directly: bumping
# to 15.5.2 or 15.5.15 both produce a real build failure ("The
# following routes were not configured to run with the Edge Runtime:
# /_not-found"), not just a stale peer-range warning. Re-evaluate once
# next-on-pages ships a release that actually supports a patched
# Next.js version — this is a real gap, not a permanently accepted one.
